Without the previous sanction of the Government, you must not ([CCS (Conduct) Rules 1964, Rule 15(1), PDF p. 11](https://dopt.gov.in/sites/default/files/CCS_Conduct_Rules_1964_Updated_27Feb15_0.pdf#page=11)):

- engage directly or indirectly in any trade or business ([CCS (Conduct) Rules 1964, Rule 15(1)(a), PDF p. 11](https://dopt.gov.in/sites/default/files/CCS_Conduct_Rules_1964_Updated_27Feb15_0.pdf#page=11));
- negotiate for or take up any other employment ([CCS (Conduct) Rules 1964, Rule 15(1)(b), PDF p. 11](https://dopt.gov.in/sites/default/files/CCS_Conduct_Rules_1964_Updated_27Feb15_0.pdf#page=11));
- hold an elective office, or canvass for a candidate, in any body ([CCS (Conduct) Rules 1964, Rule 15(1)(c), PDF p. 11](https://dopt.gov.in/sites/default/files/CCS_Conduct_Rules_1964_Updated_27Feb15_0.pdf#page=11));
- canvass for an insurance or commission agency owned or managed by a family member ([CCS (Conduct) Rules 1964, Rule 15(1)(d), PDF p. 11](https://dopt.gov.in/sites/default/files/CCS_Conduct_Rules_1964_Updated_27Feb15_0.pdf#page=11));
- take part, except in official duty, in the registration, promotion or management of a bank, a company or a commercial co-operative society ([CCS (Conduct) Rules 1964, Rule 15(1)(e), PDF p. 11](https://dopt.gov.in/sites/default/files/CCS_Conduct_Rules_1964_Updated_27Feb15_0.pdf#page=11));
- take part in making a sponsored media programme, a Government-commissioned programme produced by a private agency, or a privately produced programme, unless you take part in a Government media programme in your official capacity ([CCS (Conduct) Rules 1964, Rule 15(1)(f), PDF p. 11](https://dopt.gov.in/sites/default/files/CCS_Conduct_Rules_1964_Updated_27Feb15_0.pdf#page=11)).
